From: Herrie <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] makefile: downgrade GCC 14 default errors to warnings

GCC 14 promotes several long-standing C warnings to errors by default
(-Werror=implicit-function-declaration, int-conversion,
incompatible-pointer-types, ...). This legacy LK codebase predates
those defaults and trips them in multiple files (e.g. arch/arm/mmu.c
calling arch_clean_cache_range() without including arch/ops.h).
Downgrade them back to warnings, matching the existing -fcommon
accommodation for GCC 10.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 makefile | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/makefile
+++ b/makefile
@@ -55,6 +55,8 @@
 CFLAGS := -O2 -g -fno-builtin -finline -Wno-multichar -Wno-unused-parameter -Wno-unused-function $(LKLE_CFLAGS) -include $(CONFIGHEADER)
 # -fcommon is needed to build this using GCC 10
 CFLAGS += -fcommon
+# GCC 14 turns these into errors by default; this codebase predates that
+CFLAGS += -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=implicit-int -Wno-error=int-conversion -Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types -Wno-error=return-mismatch
 #CFLAGS += -Werror
 ifeq ($(EMMC_BOOT),1)
   CFLAGS += -D_EMMC_BOOT=1
